<title>BELGIUM: EU set to cut beef export refunds by 10 percent.</title>
<headline>EU set to cut beef export refunds by 10 percent.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-01-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>European Union beef export refunds are to be cut by 10 percent across the board this week, a senior European Commission official said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The decision, reversing an earlier one not to cut refunds, follows a flood of applications for licences which reached 60,000 in one day on Friday, the official told Reuters.</p>
<p>&quot;That figure is four times our normal weekly level. We had closed applications for licences but re-opened them again. But there were just too many and we have been forced to make a 10 percent cut across the board,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>Tenders for exports for beef will be decided by the EU beef management committee on Friday.</p>
<p>--Brussels newsroom +32 2 287-6830</p>
